# Git commits

When creating commits in this project:

- **Never** include `Co-authored-by: Cursor` or any Cursor/AI co-author trailer in the commit message.
- Keep commit messages **short and easy to understand** — a reader should know what was completed from the subject alone.
- Prefer one focused change per commit when practical.
- Use a concise subject (about 50–72 chars). Add a brief body only when needed to explain why.

## Examples

```text
✅ Fix toggle OFF race before interceptors attach
✅ Scope send-button input lookup to the form
✅ Add subjective cue exclusions to classifier

❌ Add Concise-AI Chrome extension MVP.

Implements rule-based intent classification...
Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
```
